From: "github-actions[bot]" <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:35:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: scope histogram/counter temporality limitation to
 collector ES exporter

The delta-only temporality limitation for histograms no longer applies
universally. Both delta and cumulative temporality are now supported
for histograms and counters when using the Managed OTLP endpoint
(Stack 9.5+, already on serverless). The limitation is now scoped to
the collector Elasticsearch exporter path only.

Related to #648

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md b/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
index 83c913a..3891737 100644
--- a/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
+++ b/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
@@ -58,9 +58,18 @@ When collecting host metrics through a distribution of the OTel Collector other
 
 ## Metrics data ingestion
 
-### Histograms in delta temporality only
+### Histogram and counter temporality
 
-Ingestion of OpenTelemetry metrics with the type [`Histogram`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#histogram) are only supported with [`delta temporality`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#temporality). Histograms with `cumulative` temporality are dropped before being ingested into {{es}}.
+```{applies_to}
+stack: ga 9.5
+serverless: ga
+```
+
+When you send data using the [Managed OTLP endpoint](/reference/managed-inputs/managed-otlp-endpoint.md), both [`delta` and `cumulative` temporality](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#temporality) are supported for [`Histogram`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#histogram) and counter metrics. Refer to [Metric temporality](docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality) for details, including the requirement that `xpack.otel_data.histogram_field_type` be set to `exponential_histogram` (the default since 9.4) for cumulative temporality histograms.
+
+The following limitation applies only to `Histogram` metrics ingested through the **collector Elasticsearch exporter**, not through the Managed OTLP endpoint:
+
+If you ingest data using the **collector Elasticsearch exporter** instead, only `delta` temporality is supported for `Histogram` metrics. Histograms with `cumulative` temporality are dropped before being ingested into {{es}}.
 
 Make sure to export histogram metrics with delta temporality or use the [`cumulativetodelta processor`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/processor/cumulativetodeltaprocessor) as a workaround to convert the temporality for histogram metrics.
 
